  "id": "continuing-bond",
  "term": "continuing bond",
  "definition": "A continuing bond is the ongoing psychological connection a bereaved person has with someone who has died. In grief counselling, it refers to helping the survivor restore or strengthen that inner relationship when the death has disrupted it.",
